; structural termination: a proper subtree has strictly fewer leaves than the whole tree -- count l < count(Node l r).
; count(Node l r) = count l + count r, and count r > 0 (count-positive), so count l < count l + count r. The witness is the predecessor of count r supplied by the count-positive proof. This is the `decreases` obligation a verifier discharges to admit structural recursion on a tree: every recursive descent strictly shrinks the measure (the right subtree is symmetric via commutativity).
